> pickup off. just what is a grid bug?

Grid bugs are the nasties from ChipWits, an amusing and somewhat educational
game that ran on early Macintoshen.  The object was to program a little robot
(in a pictorial language called IBOL) to navigate a maze, pick up objects and
zap grid bugs.  I often think about taking this idea and applying it to an
arbitrarily complex virtual universe, and allowing the basic guts to be in C
with basic routines like look(), move() and turn() linked in.  The "context
switches" to run active parts of the environment could be put inside these
routines.  You could potentially end up with something that's a cross between
ChipWits, NetHack and Core Wars.  Someone stop me before I actually start
coding this monstrosity!

